WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
[ YouTube Learning ]

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:04.420
Now that we know what

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.660
Google Drive within Google Classroom is,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.420
let’s move on to using

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.040
the tools that we could use to teach our students

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.720
and also check for their understanding.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:16.660
[ Don't Memorise intro music ]

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.680
Now we are in the class

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.280
that we had created earlier.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:22.880
Let me create the Google Meet link

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.820
for the live class now!

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.080
You can see the

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.240
Generate Meet link option here.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.180
Clicking on the link will auto-generate

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.760
a Google Meet link for me!

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.980
And I can make the Meet link visible to students

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.720
maybe 5 minutes before my live lesson begins.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.020
Let’s make it “Not Visible” for now.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.160
When I go back to the Stream section,

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:45.520
I will see the link here,

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.440
and this icon tells me

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.960
that the students can still not see it.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.880
I can change that 5 minutes before my class

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.620
by clicking on the Settings option

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.120
and enabling this.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.060
It’s also safe

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.160
to make it visible to my students earlier,

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.140
because the students will not be able to enter

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:05.840
the Meet class unless I am present in it.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:08.640
So it’s entirely up to each one of us!

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.660
And as we’ve seen before,

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.560
there are plenty of things we could do

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:13.440
with Google Meet,

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.100
We could share our screen

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.800
to show beautiful presentations.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.900
or we could also use the Chat feature

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.740
to engage with our students and so on.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:23.500
Now we’re just left with

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.500
material we need to add for students

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.960
that they could view AFTER my Live Class

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.520
and of course, checking for their understanding.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:34.140
Let’s go back to the Google Classroom Page

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.140
and then to the ClassWork section.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.580
I can then move on to Clicking on Create,

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.080
and then Material.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.140
Then I will enter the

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.620
appropriate title and the description.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.040
To add files,

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.260
I will click on Google Drive,

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.140
and then select more than 1 file at once.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.940
I will simply click on Control,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.040
hold the key,

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:01.780
and select the files we want to import,

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.060
and then click on Add.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.020
I can see the 3 postclass files here.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.180
What else can I do for my students?

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:14.340
Well, I could also add a link to a reliable website.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:15.780
And guess what,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.800
I have an option to also add

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.780
a YouTube link by searching for a good video!

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.020
We’re now ready with

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.180
all the material our students need.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:25.860
Within material,

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.860
I need to be sure about 2 things.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.360
One, it should belong to the relevant topic.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.720
And second, as the material should be accessible

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.500
only after my live lecture,

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.420
I will schedule the post

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.260
at a time AFTER my live lecture!

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.720
So I will schedule it on this day at 11AM.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:47.300
My students will not be able to see this

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.300
until the scheduled date!

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.100
Now after my live class

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.300
how do I know for sure if my students

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.120
have really understood the concepts

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:57.860
It’s very easy.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.960
I can click on the Classwork tab,

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.460
and then on create.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.240
I will then pick from

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.080
any of the 3 options here.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.240
I could choose a long form assignment,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.060
or a graded assignment

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.300
or I could also choose

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.020
to ask just a single question to my students.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.500
Let’s assume I gave my students a Quiz Assignment

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.920
which had 5 questions,

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.660
with each question worth 2 points!

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.060
After my students have attempted the quiz,

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.960
I also get the summary of the quizzes taken

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:28.320
in my class

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:30.320
by clicking on the Grades section here!

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.400
Clicking on any of the quiz links here

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.000
will give me a detailed summary of the scores.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.980
Here I can see that

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.020
ALL my students have

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.440
turned their assignments in!

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.560
If it’s a quiz assignment,

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:45.880
then I will make sure

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.640
I don’t forget to import grades

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.220
so that the scores are recorded.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.060
I can now see that all students

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:52.980
have got their scores!

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.540
And after this is done,

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.400
I will select all students,

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.360
and return the scores to them by clicking here.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:03.220
They will then be notified of their scores!

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.440
Here I can see that

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.160
all my students have been graded.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.780
That’s how easy it is to

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.220
replicate your School classroom on Google Classroom!

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.760
It’s seamless!

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.360
It helps you teach, collaborate, communicate,

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.860
and organise assessments in a paperless way!

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:21.780
Happy Teaching!

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:29.140
[ #TeachFromAnywhere ]

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.840
[ YouTube Learning ]

